"options":["$11 R T$","$15 R T$","$8 R T$","$R T$"],"answer":0,"solution":"Total energy\n$\\mathrm{U}=2 \\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{n}_{1}}{2} \\mathrm{RT}\\right)+4\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{n}_{2}}{2} \\mathrm{RT}\\right)$ For $\\mathrm{O}_{2}$, $\\mathrm{n}=5$ and for  $\\mathrm{Ar} , \\mathrm{n}_{2}= 3\\therefore \\mathrm{U}=2\\left(\\frac{5}{2} \\mathrm{RT}\\right)+4\\left(\\frac{3}{2} \\mathrm{RT}\\right)=11  \\mathrm{RT}$","difficulty":"Medium","source":"VITEEE 2013","_marksId":"64e45903ec226f2f4360a814"},{"id":117574,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Kinetic Theory of Gases","exam":"Engineering","examName":"VITEEE","q":"Graph of specific heat at constant volume for a monatomic gas is","options":["<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fviteee%252F2CAEQZaaXS0ylmQzfynuwvOl0fxfe9HU65Hn2guqago.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fviteee%2F2CAEQZaaXS0ylmQzfynuwvOl0fxfe9HU65Hn2guqago.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fviteee%2F2CAEQZaaXS0ylmQzfynuwvOl0fxfe9HU65Hn2guqago.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\">","<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fviteee%252FHFXyXiawDhXDHLEtWh6QGs85kfRwAGgcxwr7v4MFIUo.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fviteee%2FHFXyXiawDhXDHLEtWh6QGs85kfRwAGgcxwr7v4MFIUo.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasesto