/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fviteee%2FPTzBxzf7-zNaZuWDu4gJuktikaMKlqnJLomMZXd0Iw4.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fviteee%2FPTzBxzf7-zNaZuWDu4gJuktikaMKlqnJLomMZXd0Iw4.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\">","difficulty":"Medium","source":"VITEEE 2017","_marksId":"64e45934ec226f2f4360a9f0"},{"id":117575,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Kinetic Theory of Gases","exam":"Engineering","examName":"VITEEE","q":"The root mean square velocity of hydrogen molecules at $300 \\mathrm{ K}$ is $1930 \\mathrm{metre} / \\mathrm\\sec$. Then the r.m.s velocity of oxygen molecules at $1200 \\mathrm{ K}$ will be","options":["482.5 metre/sec","$965 \\mathrm{metre} / \\mathrm\\sec$","1930 metre/sec","3860 metre/sec"],"answer":1,"solution":"Root-mean square-velocity is given by\n\n$\\begin{aligned}& \\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{rms}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{3 R T}{M}} \\text{ i.e., } \\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{rms}} \\propto \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{T}}{\\mathrm{M}}\\right)}\\\\\n& \\frac{\\left(\\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{rms}}\\right) \\mathrm{O}_2}{\\left(\\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{rms}}\\right) \\mathrm{H}_2}=\\sqrt{\\left[\\frac{\\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{O}_2}}{\\mathrm{ T}_{\\mathrm{H}_2}} \\times \\frac{\\mathrm{M}_{\\mathrm{H}_2}}{\\mathrm{M}_{\\mathrm{O}_2}}\\right]}\\\\\n& =\\sqrt{\\left[\\left(\\frac{1200}{300}\\right) \\times\\left(\\frac{2}{32}\\right)\\right]}=\\frac{1}{2}\\\\\n& \\therefore \\quad\\left(\\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{rms}}\\right) \\mathrm{O}_{2}=\\left(\\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{rms}}\\right) \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\times \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1930}{2}=\\end{aligned}965m/s$","difficulty":"Easy","source":"VITEEE 2021","_marksId":"64e45958ec226f2f4360ab4c"}]}